  "postprocessing_amplification": {
    "identifier_digits": 7,
    "clips_affected": 0,
    "identifiers_reconstructed": 0,
    "cases": [],
    "mechanism": "A spoken number can arrive as digit words. The privacy model misses some of those - it is the same leak the entity outcomes already count - and the display renderer, which by design runs after masking, then rewrites the surviving words into a numeral. No new information escapes; the information that escaped becomes machine readable.",
    "scope": "Display only. app/digit_normalizer.py is documented as a render-time transform: storage, Onkith and the preview's own arithmetic keep the original text, so the reconstruction reaches the terminal and the JSON display_text field, not the database."
  },
  "failure_attribution": {
    "stt_caused": 5,
    "stt_caused_but_still_masked": 15,
    "privacy_model_caused": 7,
    "protected": 33,
    "postprocessing_amplified": 0,
    "interpretation": "stt_caused: the entity did not survive recognition and nothing was masked where it went. privacy_model_caused: the entity was recognizable in the transcript and the model did not mask it, or masked only part of it. Both are end-to-end leaks; only the second is a privacy-model defect. postprocessing_amplified counts a third thing, and it is not a fourth kind of leak: a leak already counted above that the render step rewrote into a numeral, which is why it is reported separately rather than added to the totals."
  }
